<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aelia Capitolina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 130–4th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aelia Capitolina was the Roman colony founded by the emperor Hadrian on the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> around 130 CE, with a temple to Jupiter Capitolinus. The plan is often seen as a cause of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bar-kokhba">Bar Kokhba</a> revolt of 132–135, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> were barred from the city. The name remained in official use for centuries, surviving in early Islamic times as Iliya.</p></div>
